Revision history for agent-construction-kit

{{$NEXT}}
    - Add claude-with, the launcher behind every starter: it loads a provider
      definition, finds the key, sets the environment and starts Claude Code.
      Definitions ship for MiniMax, Moonshot AI Kimi, Ollama Cloud, Fireworks
      AI and OpenAI through claude-code-proxy.
    - Add ack-wrappers, which creates, tests and removes the starters
      (claude_with_<name>), opens the key file in an editor, changes provider
      values and adds starters for local model servers.
    - Add ack-proxy, which reports on the claude-code-proxy behind the openai
      provider, lists its models, checks the model slots and sets up a user
      service on Linux.
    - Add ack-doctor, a read-only check of the machine: Claude Code, git, the
      plugins agent teams build on, optional tools and the installed starters.
    - Add the agent-construction-kit skill, which sets up a machine in plain
      questions: prerequisites, a starter per provider, OpenAI through the
      proxy, and local models.
    - Find claude-code-proxy in ~/.local/bin and ~/bin when it is not on PATH
      (or at ACK_PROXY_BIN); ack-proxy status and ack-doctor say so, and the
      sign-in hints then carry the full path.
    - ack-proxy check-slots checks the small-model slot too.
    - ack-wrappers new-local tells you to pass --replace when the definition
      is its own; ack-wrappers --help prints the whole header.
    - ack-wrappers install reports "path pending" instead of "path missing"
      once path-fix has added the directory to the shell profile.
    - Build an agent team for a project: the skill reads the folder, asks what
      it could not read, shows a plan, and after a yes writes the agents, the
      project skill, the rules, the board and the CLAUDE.md section, checks
      the result and commits it.
    - Add ack-repo: inspect reads a folder and changes nothing (git, branch,
      remotes, tests, sibling projects, an existing team, accounts of git
      services), init creates the repository, disk-remote puts a copy on a
      second drive. A folder inside another repository, or below a home
      folder kept in git, is reported as such and gets a repository of its
      own with init --own; init and disk-remote never run on the home folder,
      and disk-remote only on a repository of its own. A .git that git
      refuses to read (dubious ownership, a broken link, an empty folder) is
      reported with its reason, and init then writes nothing.
    - Add ack-team check, which verifies a team: agent files, the skills they
      name, rules, settings, board, CLAUDE.md, git (with the reason when git
      refuses the repository), and one run of the briefing hook per agent:
      the hook of the installed, enabled briefing plugin, never another copy
      in the cache. On Git for Windows the hook's briefing-preload.exe runs,
      or the script under the Python 3 that ack-doctor finds.
    - A board without installing anything: BOARD.md, a table per column. karr
      is offered in the board question, recommended for a family of projects,
      and installed after a yes.
    - A preset (a skill with an answer sheet) can fix answers and add skills
      per role; the team build installs the sources, bundles and skills it
      names, not its starters, which the hand-over offers.
    - Teams for folders without code: a reading check instead of a test
      command, no test-writer.
    - The machine setup moved from SKILL.md to references/machine.md.
    - ack-doctor reports Node.js and Python 3, which the skilletor and
      briefing plugins need before a team can be built or run.
